From 3e709b428d3146f3ae73bc9b4f51cff06fc73cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 10:34:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PENDING: spi: geni-msm: Reconfigure SPI mode after resume

Initialize last_mode to an invalid value (0xFF) during system resume to
ensure proper hardware reconfiguration.

Previously, last_mode was reset to 0, which caused the driver to skip
reconfiguration when the client requested SPI mode 0 (CPOL=0, CPHA=0).
This led to incorrect hardware state after Deep Sleep Quick Boot (DSQB).
Setting last_mode to 0xFF guarantees that any valid mode request after
resume is treated as a change and triggers the necessary update.

Change-Id: Ic89673d16f9c562fa99f45251298961268365387
Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index a822da072f4a..d0cd45036c2e 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -1437,7 +1437,12 @@ static int __maybe_unused spi_geni_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM) {
 		dev_dbg(dev, "%s: In S2R\n", __func__);
 		mas->cur_xfer_mode = GENI_SE_INVALID;
-		mas->last_mode = 0;
+
+		/*
+		 * Initialize last_mode to 0xFF during system resume
+		 * to force hardware reconfiguration after DSQB.
+		 */
+		mas->last_mode = 0xFF;
 		ret = spi_geni_init(mas);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
-- 
